; preflight-run.fk — the runnable door for observe/preflight.fk.
;
; WHY THIS EXISTS, and it is a finding rather than a convenience.
; The practice landed in AGENTS.md as `(pf-report "path")` — an EXPRESSION.
; Asked to follow the repo's practice from a blank context, grok found it, used
; it, and reported the one thing that was missing: "How to invoke preflight as a
; one-liner is only shown as (pf-report "…"), not a full fkwu recipe. I
; had to write a tiny driver." Every reader was going to write that same driver,
; at exactly the moment they were already dealing with something broken. A
; practice that costs a scaffold before it can be used will be skipped when it
; is most needed.
;
; Direct-source Form does not read argv (bootstrap/ground-recursive.fk says so
; plainly), so the target arrives in a file:
;
;   echo cognition/tests/your-band.fk > /tmp/preflight-target
;   ./fkwu observe/preflight-run.fk
;
; PROOF LEVEL: FOURTH-ARM ONLY — preflight shells out to compare kernels (print_str pf-arm-mask 8; host-exec 9; probed 2026-09-03).
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/preflight.fk

(do
    (defn pfr-target-file () "/tmp/preflight-target")
    (defn pfr-trim-loop (s n)
        (if (le n 0) ""
            (if (str_eq (substring s (sub n 1) n) "\n") (pfr-trim-loop s (sub n 1))
                (substring s 0 n))))
    (defn pfr-target ()
        (if (eq (fs_exists (pfr-target-file)) 0) ""
            (pfr-trim-loop (read_file (pfr-target-file))
                           (str_len (read_file (pfr-target-file))))))
    (defn pfr-scan ()
        (do (let t (pfr-target))
            (if (eq (str_len t) 0)
                (list "preflight-run: write the target path to /tmp/preflight-target first" 0)
                (pf-scan t))))
    ; PRINT IT, do not merely RETURN it — this door was mute for its whole life.
    ; Witnessed 2026-08-03: `./fkwu --src observe/preflight-run.fk` printed `5171` on a clean cell
    ; and `11846` on a cell with an unresolved call. Both are the interned pool index of a string
    ; BUILT AT RUNTIME; a string LITERAL in the same position printed its text. That looked like a
    ; live kernel defect and was NOT: the C source had carried the string-value band since
    ; 2026-07-31 (fk_sbase / fk_strv / fk_pv_root, runtime/fkwu-uni.c:5731-5747, which asks the
    ; VALUE its kind instead of guessing from the root NODE). The ./fkwu binary on disk was built
    ; hours BEFORE that landed, and binary-freshness-band answered a green 15 on it — the canary
    ; slept, so two organs were read as broken instead. The band now carries a bit for exactly this
    ; (verdict 31); rebuilding the binary makes both doors speak on their own.
    ;
    ; print_str stays regardless, and not as a workaround: a door whose whole job is to report
    ; should SAY its report, not leave it to whatever the trailing-value printer decides. The value
    ; is still returned so a caller can fold on it.
    ;
    ; AND THE EXIT CODE SAYS THE SAME THING THE PAGE SAYS.
    ; AGENTS.md item 9 asks a reader to read the exit code rather than the number, and this
    ; door — the one that carries that practice — exited 0 on every answer it ever gave. A .bml
    ; got no compile lane at all and left 0 behind; a prelude FILE that was simply absent made
    ; fkwu refuse with exit 2 and left 0 behind. A caller scripting preflight was reading a
    ; constant. `pf-scan` computes the page and the one bit from ONE fresh compile, and
    ; form_error — the body's own voice of refusal, exit nonzero — carries the bit out. The page
    ; is printed FIRST and unconditionally, so the refusal never costs the reader the reading.
    (do (let scan (pfr-scan))
        (print_str (nth scan 0))
        (if (eq (nth scan 1) 1) 0
            (form_error "preflight: no readable verdict — read the chain line above"))))
